    "body": "> Ah, yes. Demo showing a new `History` object is created when a new `Document` is created with a `javascript:` URL: https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/13653\n\nWell, a `javascript:` URL navigation creates both a new `Window` and a new `Document`, so it would certainly create a new `History`.\n\nThe initial `about:blank` case is the only case where we have a mismatch between `Window` and `Document` lifetimes. It's not clear whether `History` is matches the `Document` lifetime or the `Window` lifetime, but matching `Window` lifetime would be more normal.\n\nI think the fix from the OP is probably a good tentative direction, pending more testing on basically ~all global objects in the initial `about:blank` case.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
