    "updated_at": "2025-04-10T02:05:50Z",
    "body": "I guess the issue is that you are testing navigating to a `javascript:` URL *from the initial `about:blank`.* So in your particular case, per the current spec, we don't create a new `Window` (or a new `History`).\n\nBut that's the topic of #3267: it seems like sometimes browsers don't actually reuse the `Window` when navigating from the initial `about:blank`, despite what the current spec says.\n\nMy instinct is that we should update the spec to use \"relevant global object's associated Document\" for this step, so that it makes sense and is consistent with the rest of the `History` object's access. I will post a PR to do that.\n\nFrom there, the steps are:\n\n- Resolve #3267 by figuring out when `Window` reuse actually should happen in browsers\n- Test all global-ish objects to see whether they're attached to `Window` or `Document`, and spec them accordingly",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
